{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/336965-the-newly-deceased-cauls","id":336965,"title":"The newly deceased: cauls","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-11T05:52:58-08:00","id":336965,"title":"The newly deceased: cauls","content":"Some questions regarding the newly deceased. Would love to get insights both on RAW, and game experiences and houserules.<br /> <br /> A new wraith arrives in the shadowlands.<br /> <br /> 1) I am almost sure the new ghost first appears in the shadowlands near its highest fetter, but can't find where it says that. Or is it at the spot of death? How long after death the wraith appears in the shadowlands? Immediately?<br /> <br /> 2) A Wraith still in its caul is like a drone, attached to its place of death or fetter? Or the dreamlike state and dimmed perception is of a different kind? Have you set any rule to represent it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T07:17:22-08:00","id":336990,"title":"","content":"1) Site of their death. Wraiths end up near a fetter after coming out of a Harrowing. And a wraith appears pretty much immediately after their death.<br /> <br /> 2) The latter, a wraith in a caul is in dream-like state until reaped. There aren't rules as far as I can recall, there's nothing really there for anything to be rolled. At most its a roleplaying experience, nothing really else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T23:03:06-08:00","id":339765,"title":"","content":"While we are on the topic, I remember reading somewhere that there may be some use for a caul if a wraith chooses to save it. I don't know if it has something to do with becoming Risen or not...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}